"""The storyboard's source (BRIEF.md step 3). `tools/storyboard.py build` turns it into shots.json and
STORYBOARD.md, snapping every time to the beat grid in production/analysis/song.json and every
Seedance window to the word times in production/analysis/words.json.

Times are bar positions: bar 0 is the first drop, bar 35.5 is beat 3 of bar 35, and quarters of a
beat (sixteenths) are the finest cut. A shot runs from its `at` to the next shot's `at`.

Lyric lines are numbered as in words.json (0-78). Each line is listed once, on the shot where its
first word falls, with its type mode (masthead, coverline, subtitle, serif (the breakdown's
subtitle), mass) and text zone (left, right, top, bottom, center, ui).

Plates are Midjourney stills (production/storyboard/mj_prompts.md is built from them); clips are
Seedance windows (speak: the vocal stem; motion and dancer: the full mix). Once shots.json exists
it is the source of truth for every shot's status; rebuilding keeps the statuses it holds.
"""

